  "repeats": [],
  "notes": [
   "Parts are unchanged from step 1.",
   "The shield is stacked on the Uno, so each shield pin is joined and electrically connected to the matching Uno header pin. These are D12 DIR_A, D3 PWM_A, D9 BRAKE_A, A0 sense A, D13 DIR_B, D11 PWM_B, D8 BRAKE_B, A1 sense B, GND and VIN.",
   "The motor is on channel A (MOTOR_A+ / MOTOR_A-). It is a symmetric two-wire motor, and the image shows the orange lead on A+ and the black lead on A-. Motor port 1 goes to A+ and port 2 to A-.",
   "The battery holder's red lead goes to the shield VIN screw terminal and its black lead to GND. Both are screw terminals.",
   "The two 18650 cells sit in the holder in series: cell1 + goes to the holder positive lead, cell1 - goes to cell2 +, and cell2 - goes to the holder negative lead. This is an assumption. The holder's internal wiring is not in the catalogue.",
   "The USB cable is joined to the Uno with no port named, because the catalogue's Uno entry has no USB port. The computer is not modelled.",
   "The shield's VIN sits on the same net as the Uno's VIN through the stacked header. The external 7.4 V supply is within the shield's 5-12 V range."
  ]
 },
